Prepare a salt or brine feed for the actual downstream chemical duty (@ic-brine: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @industrial-chemistry, #source "../sources/Chlor-Alkali-Production-BREF.lingua#r_69QNQ29VT4NA2MXHTVWDNP8T2W", #source "../sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR", #source "../sources/Inorganic-Solids-and-Others-BREF.lingua#r_1M61GTSHDW8CPV4PNH48PTB4Y4", #industrial-chemistry "Chlor-alkali-cells-co-products-energy-and-quality.lingua#r_4QSMP063PRGB1934XC88JC9F63") { r_1VB0Q55CFB2PPH5VYGY5Y2VCRQ
**Read:** [Production of Chlor-alkali, BREF CAK](../sources/Chlor-Alkali-Production-BREF.lingua#r_69QNQ29VT4NA2MXHTVWDNP8T2W), the entire salt preparation, brine purification, resaturation and return-stream treatment; [Inorganic Chemical Technology — Nanda Kishore, NPTEL](../sources/Inorganic-Chemical-Technology-Kishore.lingua#r_77Z8T5RFYFNNXZ7XKZFKPRKDKR), the complete salt/sodium-compound production sequence; [Large Volume Inorganic Chemicals — Solids and Others Industry, BREF LVIC-S](../sources/Inorganic-Solids-and-Others-BREF.lingua#r_1M61GTSHDW8CPV4PNH48PTB4Y4), the relevant whole salt and solid-product accounts.

A brine contains dissolved species, suspended material and water with a particular source/history. Calcium, magnesium, sulfate, organics and trace constituents can matter to an electrochemical, crystallization or other process even when sodium chloride dominates the bulk composition. Define the impurity panel and physical support of each measurement.

Preparation may involve dissolution, clarification, chemical treatment, filtration, ion exchange or other operations justified by the feed and product. These steps create precipitates, regeneration streams and returned water/salt inventories. A purified concentration result alone cannot account for chemical consumption or impurity fate.

Source and seasonal variability, evaporation/crystallization, returned process brine and water quality can change the feed entering the next unit. Dissolved ions and the compounds used to report them need compatible charge/element balances. Distinguish a measured ionic panel from an assumed pairing of ions into salts.

**Work:** reconstruct a complete public brine-preparation system, independently closing sodium/chloride, water, charge and a consequential impurity. Compare two feed sources or purification trains at the same downstream requirement. Explain representative sampling, measurement uncertainty, residuals and the observation that would reveal impurity breakthrough or a misleading bulk-purity claim.

